मङ्ख मङ्ख, अस्, m. = मगध, a royal
bard or panegyrist; a mendicant of a particular order;
N. of a man.

माङ्गल्य, अस्, आ (?) , अम्, = मङ्गल्य, conferring
happiness, auspicious; (अस्), m. Ægle Marmelos;
(अम्), n. an auspicious thing, amulet; a benediction;
an auspicious or festive ceremony, festivity, festival;
prosperity, happiness, welfare, propitiousness.
—माङ्-
गल्य-मृदङ्ग, अस्, m. a tabour or drum beaten
on festive occasions.
—माङ्गल्यार्हा (˚य-अर्˚), f.
a species of plant (= त्रायमाणा).

मङ्क्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who dives or plunges,
diving, plunging, bathing, performing ablutions;
drowning.

